  "review": "The fixture helper defaults to exact Current D657 and rejects requests for D276/legacy identifiers in that profile. Explicit legacy mode materializes D276 and refuses D657. A focused test checks Current selected IDs, creates simultaneous D657/D276 and asserts ambiguous authority failure, then checks explicit legacy selection has D276 and no D657. Existing call sites changed to legacy were using the former helper, which already materialized D276/D274/D482: this preserves their historical fixture baseline, rather than shifting previous D657 coverage to legacy. The two explicitly Current type-inventory tests still remove D276 and install D657, and retain fail-closed rejection checks. No production validator/registry edits are part of this fixture diff.",
  "limitations": "Most pre-existing scenario fixtures remain explicitly legacy; their passing does not prove equivalent scenario coverage for D657/current-format carriers. The new Current test exercises authority-context selection and ambiguity, not every caller or full end-to-end admission. Root reports 16 modules, 124 tests, no failures/skips; no independent suite was run in this review.",
